# Project Guidelines

## Tech Stack
- Python 3.10+ with strict type hints
- FastAPI for API development
- Jinja2 for server-side rendering
- TailwindCSS for styling
- Pytest for testing (async support via pytest-asyncio)

## Code Style & Formatting
- Follow PEP 8, but enforce line length of 119 via Black
- Use `isort` with black profile for import sorting
- Docstrings must follow NumPy style
- Type hints are mandatory for all public functions and methods
- Avoid `Any` type unless strictly necessary
- Use f-strings for string formatting

## FastAPI & Async Patterns
- Prefer async/await for I/O bound operations
- Use FastAPI's `Request` and `Response` models appropriately
- Implement rate limiting with `slowapi` where applicable
- Keep endpoints thin; delegate logic to service layers or utility functions
- Use Pydantic models for request/response validation

## Templating & Frontend
- Jinja2 templates should be kept minimal and semantic
- Use TailwindCSS utility classes for styling
- JavaScript should be vanilla ES6+, kept minimal and unobtrusive
- Ensure templates are safe against XSS by default

## Project Structure
- `src/` contains the main application code
- `src/server/` handles FastAPI app, routers, and configurations
- `src/placeholder/` contains the core business logic (rename during setup)
- `tests/` contains pytest test suite
- Use relative imports within packages, absolute imports for external modules

## Pre-commit & CI
- All changes must pass pre-commit hooks (black, isort, pylint, etc.)
- CI runs on Python 3.10 to 3.13
- Ensure new code includes corresponding tests
- Use `pytest.mark.asyncio` for async tests

## General
- Keep functions focused and single-responsibility
- Prioritize readability and maintainability over clever code
- Update documentation and type hints alongside code changes
- If modifying templates, verify rendering context variables are properly passed
